        <type>s32</type>
        <definition>s32 XAsu_MldsaSign</definition>
        <argsstring>(XAsu_ClientParams *ClientParamPtr, XAsu_MldsaSignVerifyParams *MldsaParamPtr)</argsstring>
        <name>XAsu_MldsaSign</name>
        <param>
          <type>XAsu_ClientParams *</type>
          <declname>ClientParamPtr</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="struct_x_asu___mldsa_sign_verify_params" kindref="compound">XAsu_MldsaSignVerifyParams</ref> *</type>
          <declname>MldsaParamPtr</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>This function sends a command to ASUFW to generate an ML-DSA signature over the provided message (pure ML-DSA or HashML-DSA, hedged or deterministic, with an optional context string). </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>ClientParamPtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to the XAsu_ClientParams structure which holds the client input parameters. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>MldsaParamPtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to the <ref refid="struct_x_asu___mldsa_sign_verify_params" kindref="compound">XAsu_MldsaSignVerifyParams</ref> structure which holds the ML-DSA signature generation parameters.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>XST_SUCCESS, if IPI request to ASU is sent successfully.</para></listitem><listitem><para>XASU_INVALID_ARGUMENT, if any argument is invalid.</para></listitem><listitem><para>XASU_INVALID_UNIQUE_ID, if the unique ID is invalid.</para></listitem><listitem><para>XST_FAILURE, if sending an IPI request to ASU fails. </para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
<para>Validate input parameters.</para><para>Validate ML-DSA signature generation parameters.</para><para>Generate a unique ID and register the callback function.</para><para>Create command header.</para><para>Update request buffer and send an IPI request to ASU. </para>        </inbodydescription>
