      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__xasu__mldsa__client__apis_1ga18c8cf02e218a342838405be0b25ba3c" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>s32</type>
        <definition>s32 XAsu_MldsaSignDerand</definition>
        <argsstring>(XAsu_ClientParams *ClientParamPtr, XAsu_MldsaSignDerandParams *MldsaParamPtr)</argsstring>
        <name>XAsu_MldsaSignDerand</name>
        <param>
          <type>XAsu_ClientParams *</type>
          <declname>ClientParamPtr</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="struct_x_asu___mldsa_sign_derand_params" kindref="compound">XAsu_MldsaSignDerandParams</ref> *</type>
          <declname>MldsaParamPtr</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>This function sends a command to ASUFW to generate an ML-DSA signature with the signing randomness rnd supplied by the caller instead of drawn from the TRNG, so that the ACVP hedged signature vectors can be driven through the module. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Hedged signing draws rnd from an approved RBG, so only an ASUFW built with CAVP support serves this command; any other build rejects it as an invalid command. The secret key must be passed by address, as the key vault is not available to this command, and the Deterministic field is ignored because the supplied rnd decides the randomness outright.</para><para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>ClientParamPtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to the XAsu_ClientParams structure which holds the client input parameters. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>MldsaParamPtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to the <ref refid="struct_x_asu___mldsa_sign_derand_params" kindref="compound">XAsu_MldsaSignDerandParams</ref> structure which holds the ML-DSA signature generation parameters and the rnd to sign with.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>XST_SUCCESS, if IPI request to ASU is sent successfully.</para></listitem><listitem><para>XASU_INVALID_ARGUMENT, if any argument is invalid.</para></listitem><listitem><para>XASU_INVALID_UNIQUE_ID, if the unique ID is invalid.</para></listitem><listitem><para>XST_FAILURE, if sending an IPI request to ASU fails. </para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
<para>Validate input parameters.</para><para>Validate ML-DSA signature generation parameters and the supplied rnd.</para><para>Generate a unique ID and register the callback function.</para><para>Create command header.</para><para>Update request buffer and send an IPI request to ASU. </para>        </inbodydescription>
